 "audit": "Cohort is a pooled mix of heterogeneous diagnosis labels: nonspecific labels (Glioma malignant, Neoplasm NOS, missing/Unknown, Medulloblastoma NOS) mix subtypes, so frequencies are blends and associations may reflect subtype composition. Several hypermutated cases (up to ~9000 genes) exist, mostly in Glioma malignant; I excluded cases with >100 mutated genes for the main analysis because they inflate gene counts. Many small diagnosis groups (n<20) limit power. Likely pooled from multiple studies with batch/pipeline differences; the PIK3R1 signal in pilocytic astrocytoma (30/168, scattered non-hotspot variants) and the scattered-variant ARID1B and ZMYM3 signals look like possible technical or cohort artifacts, so I gave them lower probabilities. Sex, age and site were not adjusted for. Many tests (~2500 pairs) so I relied on very small p-values.",
 "methods": "Per case, gene-level mutation presence (any non-synonymous variant). For each diagnosis (n>=8) and gene (>=3 mutated cases), one-sided Fisher exact test of diagnosis versus all other tumors, after excluding hypermutated cases (>100 mutated genes). Kept associations with p below about 1e-6 plus a few plausible weaker ones, checked against known biology; expected frequency from observed rate in the diagnosis; probabilities reflect significance, known literature and artifact concerns."
}